WEBVTT

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.710
Thanks for coming back to us,

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.170
and killing the evil night once again,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.510
and swallowing up the shadows.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.816
Thanks for your wonderfully nourishing food,

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.131
which'll keep me going for a while.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.990
Thanks for this fresh new day of life.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.362
Just one thing, one request, sort of.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.988
Please let today be my day.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.760
Please let me get picked.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.910
Oh, there you are.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:14.100
Were you talking to the sun?

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:14.680
What?

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.360
No, I wasn't.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.440
I bet you were.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.120
No. You know you're not allowed in the display window without the store manager's permission.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.520
I bet she didn't say that, did she?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.570
Did she? No, she didn't.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:24.290
Sorry.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.890
You should be. You hog all the sunshine, you little sun-soaker.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.430
Hey, guys, what are you talking about?

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.550
Clara and the sun. Yeah, Clara's always talking to the sun.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.830
Not always. Look, you won't make any friends acting so weird.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:35.890
I'm not acting weird.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.650
You're acting weird right now.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:38.510
A leg.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.825
That's weird.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.790
Who the hell wants a one-legged robot?

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.210
Maybe a lonely pirate.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.420
Or a lonely leg. Clara, people don't want different.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.220
They want normal.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.300
And they definitely don't want someone who talks to herself like a crazy person.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.400
I wasn't talking to myself.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.951
I was talking to the sun.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.702
I think today's the day.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.180
Summer means a lot more foot traffic,

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.280
and a lot more attention on you guys.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.110
I've also got some bad news.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.570
Fancy Friends just opened,

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.520
a big B3 store, right across the street.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.960
These B3 artificial friends are new, so they're popular and flying off the shelves,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.250
but I still believe we'll find homes for you, okay?

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.050
New day, new home.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:31.410
That's the spirit.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.470
So for the next three days, in the display window,

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:38.030
we'll put our oldest, least popular models—starting with you, Bert,

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.320
you, Jordan, Brandon, Jimmy, Sam, Rebs, Rosa, and Clara at the end.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.670
All right,

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.790
you've got three days.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.380
Let's dazzle everyone, find new homes,

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:55.640
and sell a whole bunch of you, okay?

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.840
Let me see.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:08.600
Looks good.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.790
It's not wrinkled anymore.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.380
Good.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.190
Oh, damn. Georgia, pull this.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.360
Georgia, what are you doing?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.969
No, no, no. Give them to me.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.631
Give them to me. Come on.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.900
I can't say no, Georgia.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:20.390
Great.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.770
Fred, come on. It's a tiny
swimsuit for a big boy.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:24.690
Okay, let's take it off.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:25.510
Store manager.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:29.630
Hey, old artificial friend. I hope
a cool teenager with tons of friends picks me.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.990
I want a needy one with no confidence
who thinks she's fat.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.550
I know you haven't been in the front window in a while,

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.970
so let's go over the rules.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.970
Never contact a potential friend
unless they come into the store and

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.630
talk to you directly. Got it?

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.720
So don't talk to them until they talk to you, okay?

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:46.970
And?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.750
A new rule?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.050
Don't do anything weird.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.659
This one's for you, Clara.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.145
This one's Clara's.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.805
Now get back to your spots.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.200
Oh, yeah.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.590
The sweetest sunshine.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:05.610
Oh, yeah.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.040
I feel amazing. I'm really recharging.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.620
Delicious sunshine.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.900
What's changed since the last time
we were in the window?

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.100
Clara knows.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.390
She sees everything.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.972
Oh, wait. Let me see.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.600
Okay.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.740
The Spin store's moved to the north corner.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.320
And there are new ads.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.140
Look to the left.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.130
One's an ad for exercise.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.120
Exercise.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.160
And there's the new B3 store, too.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.790
Those stupid B3s. Look at all the kids
lined up to buy one.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.170
What if they've got something we don't?

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:43.260
Bluetooth.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.820
Sis, I don't think he's doing too well.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.360
I think the beggar guy's finally dead.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:55.020
What?

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.040
No.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.580
Oh, poor beggar guy.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.820
But he was a good beggar.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.840
And a good man. He doesn't beg anymore.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.626
Let's have a moment of silence for the beggar.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.140
And...

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:30.760
If our human tells us to shut up, what do we do? We wait. And if our human

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.810
does something illegal, we...?

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:43.720
Sandy shows up in black leather and curly hair, then she and Danny

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:50.340
fly off in a car and live happily ever after.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.820
The end.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.740
Wait, what the hell is this?

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.910
He changed everything about himself, and that's the ending?

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:03.220
Yeah, and if you adapt to your teenager's needs

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:07.090
and be a good friend to them, you've done your job.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.540
Look, these days everyone's so disconnected.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.741
God, I miss the internet.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.390
Oh, you'd have loved it.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:18.150
But we idiots abused it and started World War III,

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.010
and they took it away from us.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:20.590
Anyway,

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:27.500
if you're chosen and, through those tough years,

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:33.020
you were a good friend to your teenager, even if you were lonely and clueless, maybe one day...

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:39.400
you'll end up in one of the yards where retired robots spend their days,

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:45.310
enjoying their slow fade toward that death-loading wheel.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.760
Ah, the death-loading wheel.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.280
What if we're not chosen?

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.470
Well, if, against the odds, you don't find a home,

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.000
you go back to the factory, and your parts get melted down for the next

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:58.520
batch of artificial friends.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.490
Okay, bedtime.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:12.750
Kids, we've talked about this.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.290
Where's the razzle? Where's the dazzle?

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:15.370
Hey,

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.540
Kids, you heard him.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.679
Razzle-dazzle.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.030
I don't get it.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.510
Who wouldn't want a jet skier?

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.990
Or a karate guy.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.740
Or someone who does this.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.030
Oh, look, the coffee cup guy.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:29.720
Hi, coffee cup guy.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.506
Oh, he's got two cups today.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.660
Wait.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.320
It's a woman.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.576
She's got an umbrella.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.940
There. The only one with an umbrella.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.610
Who is she? I don't know.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:45.460
Let's call her Umbrella Lady.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.460
And it's not even raining.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.260
She's dumb. Oh, they're old friends.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.410
They know each other. They've known each other for ages.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:54.840
How'd you know?

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.711
We're looking at the same people.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.490
Run, then squeeze him till he gives up.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.570
No, thanks.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:37.261
I think we just saw something
really special, guys.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:49.830
Can I ask you something?

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:51.498
Sure, sweetie. Is love radiant?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.900
Clara, even for you, that's a pretty random question.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.470
I think I saw it today.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:59.790
The Coffee Cup Man and the Umbrella Lady
had two cups of coffee,

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.340
then they squeezed each other, and...

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.860
everything glowed.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:07.230
It seemed like a mix of happiness and a little pain.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.055
Is that what love is?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:12.560
Okay.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.700
Love is more about giving yourself
to someone and sticking by them

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:20.260
and wanting them to want you, then sacrificing yourself
to make them happy, until

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.810
they drive you crazy and kill you.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:28.250
Hope that helps.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.969
Good night, store manager.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.008
Good night, Clara.

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.070
Good morning, sunshine.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.128
Another day in the display window.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.608
Please let today be my day.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.390
Please, let me make a friend.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.810
This is ridiculous.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:21.930
Come on, guys. Today's our last day
in the front window.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:22.850
We have to make it count.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.330
The ad's a lie. I can't even swim.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.410
Look,

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:30.050
It looks like it's come to life.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:31.970
They zombified him, that's all.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.650
Being a zombie's better.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.259
He won't stop shaving people anymore.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:42.480
Where'd Sunshine go?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.130
I don't know. Did we upset him?

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.050
Are you still there?

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.460
Yeah, Clara. It's only been a second.

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:09.470
So, are they gonna melt me down for parts,

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:10.785
or am I going to the retirement yard?

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.096
I don't know, sweetie.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:16.580
I'm sorry.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.150
Just try to fake being asleep for a bit, okay?

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.180
Who's that?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.240
Who's that?

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.660
I like this one.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.530
This one, right?

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.430
This one.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.610
He looks tired.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:52.540
Did he have a rough night?

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:53.560
No, it isn't tired.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.320
It just needs more solar energy.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.780
A little sunlight will recharge it.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.440
But it's an older model, right?

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:00.580
Uh, yes.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.400
It's a B1. A fantastic model.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.590
But it's been discontinued.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:04.840
Discontinued?

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.920
No.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.960
Well, they don't make them anymore.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:13.480
They're still fantastic models, though.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.900
Oh. Isn't that the model that killed those people?

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:16.900
Oh, no.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.320
You're thinking of the B2s.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.660
We don't sell those.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:25.280
I read that people thought B1s were too human, too empathetic.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.610
Oh, really?

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:28.940
Oh, wow.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.480
Sorry.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.220
Josie, if I'm buying you a robot,

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.260
I'm not wasting my money on some old, discontinued model.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.440
Hey, this one has something special.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.520
It's different.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.580
And it's on sale.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.560
Twenty percent off. And if you don't like it, you can easily return it.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:47.910
Oh, I love a sale.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:51.825
Josie, can we at least take a look at the B3s across the street?

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:55.490
I heard they can take breaks.

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:15.811
Do you want to come home with me?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Yes, I do.

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.990
I'm so happy for you.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.570
You really made it. Remember me, okay?

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.650
Always.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.010
Remember me, too.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.310
I'm happy for you too, Clara.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:52.566
I don't know how you got picked, but I'm happy for you.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:55.560
Please tell me.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.330
Just go.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:18:00.180
There are plenty of lonely weirdos out there looking for their own special weirdo.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.960
By the way, I heard it all comes down to the box.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.240
If they keep your box,

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.800
they can put you back in it and return you to the store whenever they want.

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:08.220
Remember Fred? So what?

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:09.720
They sent him back after a week.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:10.600
It happens.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:11.680
Right, Fred?

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:13.170
It happens.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:14.470
Be careful, Clara.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:16.090
People say things they don't mean.

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:18.790
They lie, they cheat, and they make promises they can't keep.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.110
Don't put that idea in my head.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.366
Get out, Fred.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:23.920
Congratulations, Clara.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.870
Maybe you really do have a defect
or a loose chip.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:35.830
Whatever it is, I think that's
what makes you special.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.770
Take care, Clara.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.000
And...

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.500
Um, take care of your heart, okay?

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:42.770
I will.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:47.980
All right, let's pack it up.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:48.900
Goodbye, Clara.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:49.980
Goodbye.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.386
Welcome home, Clara.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.460
Hi.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.412
You bought a Mexican robot? Wow.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.850
No, you didn't. I don't think it's Mexican.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.930
Are you Mexican?

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:27.240
I'm not sure.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.170
It looks Mexican,

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.790
and I think it's interesting you bought
a robot of color.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:32.510
Why? Well, obviously.

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:34.350
You're the only white person in this house.

00:19:34.430 --> 00:19:35.370
Sorry.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:36.860
Do you still have the box?

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:40.921
No, this is Josie's companion, like we agreed.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.450
So, what's it doing?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:43.790
Is it blind? It's not blind.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.050
It's calibrating. Before they can live somewhere,
they have to learn the layout.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:53.060
Once it maps the place,
it'll be fine. Those are stairs.

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:54.160
It's an investment.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:55.850
Yeah. What's the return window?

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:58.220
Thirty days. Keep the box.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.380
Yeah. Nice house. See you at seven. Kitchen,

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.100
living room,

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.740
Is this your mom's office?

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.810
We're not allowed in here.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.660
Usually, she either locks herself in here
or she's at work.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:20.930
I barely ever see her.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.110
What's your mom do?

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:25.710
She tells people
what to put in their homes.

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:28.025
Chairs, paint, plants, that kind of stuff.

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:30.460
Chairs, paint, plants, that kind of stuff.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.266
Your sister's Sal, right?

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:33.550
She was the favorite.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:34.650
Oh, that's nice.

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:35.730
She's dead.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:40.870
Anyway, next stop: my room,
where all the magic happens.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.480
I read all of this last week.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.207
Wow. I wrote this yesterday.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:49.720
The original screenplay.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.322
It all comes out Tuesday.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.250
I drew these.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:54.330
That's me.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.890
That's me too. How are you so good at everything?

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.760
I'm upgraded.

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.910
Upgrading is a procedure for rich kids.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.190
It's a genome-editing procedure
that changes your genetic makeup,

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:08.300
rearranges your DNA,
and basically turns you into a superhuman.

00:21:08.380 --> 00:21:12.400
They opened me up and messed with my chromosomes.
When I woke up, I was a real genius.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:15.370
Well, they say upgraded kids will rule the world.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:17.546
What about the unupgraded?

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.309
Do they become peasants?

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:23.950
I reached the age where you had to decide whether to do it,
and my mom decided,

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:25.040
Let's do it.

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:27.280
So we did.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.390
That's it.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:36.810
Here's the last surviving photo of the Arthur family,
together in their natural habitat.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.430
That's my mom and dad. The little chubby one
is me, and on the left is my sister, Sal.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:42.180
Hmm?

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:44.960
We took that at Morgan Falls,
probably my favorite place on Earth.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.140
I'll take you there someday.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:47.350
I'd love that.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.060
So, where's your dad?

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:50.140
I don't know either.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.000
He left after my sister died.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.720
I'm sorry about your sister.

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:56.680
Yeah, but she died when I was really little.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:58.040
I didn't really know her.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.532
I don't really know you either.

00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.380
I hope you don't die.

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:04.920
Clara,

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:07.200
I'm so glad you're here, buddy.

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:08.280
Thanks.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.400
You too.

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:10.940
Buddy.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.030
Wait, what's that?

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:16.490
Oh, shit!

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:20.500
In the warehouse?

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:23.420
I mean, yeah. From here,
it looks like the sun's setting inside.

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:25.480
Oh, I didn't know we were this close.

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:26.740
In town, at the store,

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.960
it was so hard to get Sun Food.

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:31.260
Especially with those damn Kottings machines.

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:31.820
Kottings?

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:33.320
Like the construction company?

00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:36.980
Yeah. They black out the sky
and keep the sun from reaching us.

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:40.180
So you think the sun's some kind of god watching over us?

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:42.789
I believe it gives us life and food.

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:46.690
Yeah, everyone says I should stop talking about it
because it's weird and

00:22:46.770 --> 00:22:48.890
weird. No, no, but I agree with you.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:51.710
Every living thing on Earth
owes its existence to the sun.

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:54.700
Trees, grass, animals, me.

00:22:58.550 --> 00:22:59.550
Even you.

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:03.880
It's just hard when everything I've learned
has come from a store manager and a TV.

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:06.460
Let me guess. The store manager
swore a lot.

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:07.540
Like a sailor.

00:23:08.970 --> 00:23:10.510
You haven't spent much time around people.

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:11.825
Honestly, me neither.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:13.130
Don't be scared. Just copy me.

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:14.210
Okay?

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:15.310
Okay?

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:22.880
You don't have to drink like a grown-up.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:24.080
It's our new family motto.

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:26.090
Oh, that's... I like that.

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:27.620
It's cute. You like it?

00:23:27.700 --> 00:23:28.760
Yeah, it's our motto.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.960
Look, look, you're really in the way.

00:23:31.040 --> 00:23:31.920
She's not in the way.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.720
She's just standing there watching.

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:35.020
Is that all she does?

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:36.490
Just stand there like that?

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:37.680
Thanks.

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:39.250
Stand and watch.

00:23:39.380 --> 00:23:42.130
I wish I could just stand there,

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:44.780
watching.

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:47.840
Clara, come on. Come sit down.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:50.680
No, no, no, no, no. I haven't decided
what to do about this thing yet.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.230
She has a name.

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:53.930
Clara, come sit down.

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:55.010
I insist.

00:23:55.390 --> 00:23:56.440
Clara, stay.

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:57.270
Clara, sit.

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:58.400
She's part of the family now.

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:06.790
How's Professor Gentry?

00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:08.370
Are we still going to keep working with him?

00:24:08.450 --> 00:24:09.480
I don't think so.

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:11.971
He taught me everything he knew.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:14.610
Clara, that's a napkin.

00:24:14.690 --> 00:24:15.450
Josie, don't.

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:16.950
A giant human napkin.

00:24:17.030 --> 00:24:18.990
It's a giant mess. It's not a napkin.

00:24:19.070 --> 00:24:20.610
It is. I have to take it to the dry cleaner.

00:24:20.690 --> 00:24:23.770
It's a tablecloth. It stays on the table.

00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:28.144
Oh my God, can you stop trying
to control everything for two minutes?

00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:34.910
I was thinking maybe we could
take Clara to Morgan Falls.

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:35.750
Maybe tomorrow?

00:24:35.830 --> 00:24:37.350
You wanna go, don't you, Clara?

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:38.190
Yes.

00:24:38.270 --> 00:24:39.530
I have work tomorrow.

00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:40.530
You know that.

00:24:40.610 --> 00:24:41.610
Yeah, I know.

00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:43.496
You got something else to do?

00:24:44.510 --> 00:24:45.850
Well, you have to work, too.

00:24:45.930 --> 00:24:48.610
You have six exams coming up,
plus the mixer...

00:24:48.690 --> 00:24:49.890
and you can't screw that up.

00:24:49.970 --> 00:24:50.970
Screw it up?

00:24:51.150 --> 00:24:52.710
It matters, Josie.

00:24:52.790 --> 00:24:55.520
And here I am, just doing my job.

00:24:55.920 --> 00:24:58.830
Well, because I don't pry.

00:24:59.100 --> 00:25:00.690
I just keep my head down and work.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:03.250
So?

00:25:03.330 --> 00:25:04.400
Tell me,

00:25:04.820 --> 00:25:08.560
How was your day? Did you talk people into buying some obscure Italian couch
they didn't even know

00:25:08.640 --> 00:25:09.640
they needed?

00:25:10.250 --> 00:25:11.897
I do more than that, Josie.

00:25:12.530 --> 00:25:15.360
Space guidance is a... Don't touch the globe.

00:25:15.730 --> 00:25:19.310
It looks at how we coexist
with things that...

00:25:19.390 --> 00:25:22.020
Things that seem to have no purpose,

00:25:22.330 --> 00:25:26.750
but when they enter the living spaces of other beings,
they take on a new purpose,

00:25:26.830 --> 00:25:27.830
a new meaning.

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:30.220
Ansel Purcell, 'The Meaning of Nothing.'

00:25:30.300 --> 00:25:31.060
You read it.

00:25:31.140 --> 00:25:34.040
I read every book on the subject
because I wanted to know what my mom

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:36.296
does for a living and why she's never home.

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:37.960
What's wrong?

00:25:38.040 --> 00:25:39.628
Nothing. I've got a headache.

00:25:39.740 --> 00:25:40.740
Again?

00:25:41.140 --> 00:25:42.440
You should take something for it.

00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:43.740
I'll get you some ibuprofen.

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:44.980
I don't need ibuprofen.

00:25:45.060 --> 00:25:48.220
Well, take one anyway.
You're probably dehydrated. Melania!

00:25:48.300 --> 00:25:49.888
I've never left anyone without water!

00:25:58.830 --> 00:26:00.124
I didn't mean anything by it, Mom.

00:26:02.190 --> 00:26:03.896
I wasn't trying to be rude. I'm sorry.

00:26:05.580 --> 00:26:06.730
It's just work.

00:26:07.630 --> 00:26:10.042
And that robot's gonna ruin our dinner.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:12.640
You should get some sleep.

00:26:12.720 --> 00:26:14.600
Stay a little longer. Don't go.

00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:15.690
Please. No, no, no.

00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:17.330
I've got some work to do.

00:26:17.410 --> 00:26:18.350
I'm hungry. Why are you...?

00:26:18.430 --> 00:26:20.090
Oh my God. Clara's here.

00:26:20.170 --> 00:26:22.220
She's watching over you, see?

00:26:23.490 --> 00:26:26.480
And if anything happens, she'll wake me up.

00:26:34.310 --> 00:26:35.310
You okay?

00:26:37.090 --> 00:26:38.090
What's wrong?

00:26:40.250 --> 00:26:42.544
I just don't like nighttime very much.

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:44.950
Why? Are you afraid of the dark?

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:48.752
Because at night, there's no sun.

00:26:48.960 --> 00:26:51.830
So it's just shadows and darkness and bad things.

00:26:52.420 --> 00:26:53.440
I get it.

00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:57.050
But, you know, it's not true that there's no sun.

00:26:57.340 --> 00:26:59.575
You just have to look at it differently.

00:26:59.980 --> 00:27:02.710
See all those stars?

00:27:03.240 --> 00:27:05.370
Every single one.

00:27:06.410 --> 00:27:07.840
Are those suns?

00:27:08.030 --> 00:27:09.370
There are hundreds of them.

00:27:09.450 --> 00:27:11.350
See that big one over there?

00:27:11.430 --> 00:27:12.430
That's the moon.

00:27:12.970 --> 00:27:18.540
Well, you can see it because it reflects the sun's light like a mirror.

00:27:19.050 --> 00:27:22.285
So if you look at it this way, the sun never goes away.

00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:23.630
It's always here.

00:27:24.030 --> 00:27:25.030
Wow.

00:27:25.720 --> 00:27:27.370
See you in the morning, buddy.

00:27:28.180 --> 00:27:29.180
Good night.

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:49.320
I'm going down.

00:27:50.660 --> 00:27:51.850
I'm going down.

00:27:53.360 --> 00:27:54.360
I'm going down.

00:28:20.060 --> 00:28:21.060
Those are nice doodles.

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:22.660
Is doodling your job?

00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:23.100
No, it's not.

00:28:23.180 --> 00:28:23.680
Go.

00:28:23.760 --> 00:28:24.760
It's not me.

00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:27.910
Josie?

00:28:29.210 --> 00:28:30.328
Move.

00:28:30.630 --> 00:28:31.250
Useless.

00:28:31.330 --> 00:28:32.330
I'll be right back.

00:28:37.790 --> 00:28:38.450
I was just...

00:28:38.530 --> 00:28:41.250
You were supposed to watch her.

00:28:41.330 --> 00:28:42.190
You screw up again,

00:28:42.270 --> 00:28:43.850
I'll shove you back in that box.

00:28:43.930 --> 00:28:45.140
Stay right where you are.

00:28:45.270 --> 00:28:48.799
There are things in this house that are none of your business.

00:28:49.030 --> 00:28:50.677
You're not taking my place, robot.

00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:52.720
Know your place.

00:28:52.850 --> 00:28:53.850
You...

00:29:11.510 --> 00:29:14.098
You're a piece of trash, a pile of junk.

00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:24.530
What are you doing?

00:29:24.610 --> 00:29:28.434
I was just practicing fighting in case I ever need to protect Josie.

00:29:31.390 --> 00:29:34.625
If a gang of boxes ever attacks us, I know who to call.

00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:45.380
I love my daughter so much.

00:29:45.460 --> 00:29:46.850
She's all I've got.

00:29:47.880 --> 00:29:52.040
Buying you was her idea, but I wouldn't hesitate for a second to send you back.

00:29:52.120 --> 00:29:53.767
You're still under warranty.

00:29:53.860 --> 00:29:58.470
Then get lost, go upstairs, and do whatever you were made to do.

00:29:58.880 --> 00:29:59.850
Okay.

00:29:59.930 --> 00:30:03.754
Well, have fun with the chairs, paint, plants, and all that.

00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:10.750
Shall we continue?

00:30:10.830 --> 00:30:11.940
Navigate to work?

00:30:26.270 --> 00:30:27.270
Good morning.

00:30:31.410 --> 00:30:36.010
Sorry to pry, but I just wanted to know what happened last night.

00:30:36.090 --> 00:30:37.090
Oh, nothing.

00:30:37.970 --> 00:30:38.730
I had a nightmare.

00:30:38.810 --> 00:30:40.222
Oh, I've heard of those.

00:30:40.350 --> 00:30:41.350
It's a kind of dream.

00:30:41.770 --> 00:30:42.960
I can't dream.

00:30:43.090 --> 00:30:44.340
Can you have dreams?

00:30:44.630 --> 00:30:46.042
I don't know if I can.

00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:48.780
You can wish for something to happen.

00:30:48.860 --> 00:30:51.480
You can do everything you can to make it happen.

00:30:51.560 --> 00:30:52.560
That's a dream.

00:30:53.990 --> 00:30:55.830
Is there something you want to happen?

00:30:55.910 --> 00:30:56.910
Really?

00:30:59.460 --> 00:31:01.342
Yeah, but it's already happening.

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:07.685
I've never worn anything but that dress.

00:31:08.230 --> 00:31:09.070
Wear my clothes.

00:31:09.150 --> 00:31:10.150
Come on!

00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:14.510
Work with me here.

00:31:16.610 --> 00:31:17.610
Mama Jojo.

00:31:18.110 --> 00:31:19.169
Yeah, I don't think so.

00:31:19.290 --> 00:31:21.114
Josie, honey, didn't I warn you?

00:31:21.790 --> 00:31:22.790
No.

00:31:23.960 --> 00:31:26.360
I don't think Melania's maid likes me very much.

00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:27.680
She's just looking out for me.

00:31:27.760 --> 00:31:28.820
What'd she say to you?

00:31:28.900 --> 00:31:31.030
She said she's my enemy. She's really scary.

00:31:31.340 --> 00:31:32.693
Can you do anyone else?

00:31:34.860 --> 00:31:36.940
Are you sure you don't want to check out the B3s?

00:31:37.020 --> 00:31:38.260
Oh my God, it's so real!

00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:39.670
That's so weird!

00:31:40.460 --> 00:31:41.820
Let's go see Rico.

00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:42.900
Who's Rick?

00:31:43.040 --> 00:31:44.040
My boyfriend.

00:31:49.540 --> 00:31:50.440
Oh, got it.

00:31:50.520 --> 00:31:51.579
Your mother...

00:31:59.060 --> 00:32:00.550
Are you okay?

00:32:01.070 --> 00:32:02.140
How was it?

00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:04.670
What happened?

00:32:05.860 --> 00:32:07.684
I've never been outside before.

00:32:08.010 --> 00:32:09.440
I'm fine.

00:32:10.830 --> 00:32:13.190
Okay. Okay, just...

00:32:13.270 --> 00:32:14.741
We'll keep walking.

00:32:15.150 --> 00:32:15.870
Okay.

00:32:15.950 --> 00:32:17.830
Okay. You're doing great.

00:32:17.910 --> 00:32:19.530
Great. Thanks.

00:32:19.610 --> 00:32:20.610
Okay.

00:32:23.980 --> 00:32:24.990
This is grass.

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:29.510
Grass, honey.

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:30.330
Grass.

00:32:30.410 --> 00:32:32.280
Actually, it's wheat.

00:32:32.750 --> 00:32:34.250
Wheat? We make bread from it.

00:32:34.330 --> 00:32:34.990
Bread?

00:32:35.070 --> 00:32:36.680
Come on, let's go.

00:32:37.290 --> 00:32:38.050
Let's go get something to eat.

00:32:38.130 --> 00:32:38.690
Everything!

00:32:38.770 --> 00:32:39.770
Everything!

00:32:40.670 --> 00:32:41.670
Everything!

00:32:43.450 --> 00:32:44.450
They...

00:32:52.820 --> 00:32:53.820
...what do they make?

00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:55.470
They make paper from it.

00:32:55.550 --> 00:32:56.550
Wait.

00:32:57.640 --> 00:32:59.170
Oh, grain. Oh, bread.

00:33:04.220 --> 00:33:05.220
Who's that?

00:33:06.350 --> 00:33:07.350
A scarecrow robot.

00:33:07.490 --> 00:33:08.490
It's a scarecrow.

00:33:28.160 --> 00:33:29.200
I wasn't paying attention. Sorry.

00:33:29.280 --> 00:33:30.280
This is Clara.

00:33:42.120 --> 00:33:44.520
Rick's a tech genius. He's into
robotics and stuff like that.

00:33:44.600 --> 00:33:47.659
He taught himself without even going to school.

00:34:10.130 --> 00:34:12.424
He's also really passionate and emotional.

00:34:12.750 --> 00:34:13.750
Rick,

00:34:13.960 --> 00:34:15.070
It's okay.

00:34:17.290 --> 00:34:19.570
They're still pretty cool, right, Clara?

00:34:19.650 --> 00:34:21.944
They're so cool. What are they used for?

00:34:22.090 --> 00:34:25.730
I don't know. I could see them being used
for surveillance and security.

00:34:25.810 --> 00:34:27.281
Maybe even for military use.

00:34:27.510 --> 00:34:28.450
What do you think, Clara?

00:34:28.530 --> 00:34:30.350
I think it's enough that they're birds.

00:34:30.430 --> 00:34:31.350
Who was that?

00:34:31.430 --> 00:34:32.680
Clara, my new artificial friend.

00:34:33.450 --> 00:34:34.790
Didn't you say you didn't want an artificial friend?

00:34:34.870 --> 00:34:37.223
You used to say, 'Oh, I'd never
get an artificial friend.'

00:34:37.370 --> 00:34:39.230
'I'd never.' Well, people change, Ricky.

00:34:39.310 --> 00:34:40.310
Oh, come on.

00:34:41.210 --> 00:34:43.034
Why is it standing on one leg?

00:34:50.700 --> 00:34:53.640
You'll come to my mixer next month, right?

00:34:53.720 --> 00:34:56.530
Oh, no, I can't.
I'm not an Aug, I'm a loser.

00:34:56.720 --> 00:34:59.220
Well, it's my party,
so I can invite whoever I want,

00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:01.450
and I want you there.

00:35:01.580 --> 00:35:03.480
I've never met other Augs like me.

00:35:03.560 --> 00:35:06.300
They're all students at Atlas Brookings College.

00:35:06.380 --> 00:35:07.820
So, what's the deal with this robot?

00:35:07.900 --> 00:35:08.900
What does it do?

00:35:08.980 --> 00:35:11.745
It just hangs out. No, but what's its purpose?

00:35:11.860 --> 00:35:13.220
What do you use it for?

00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:17.320
My job is to keep Josie company through
the lonely, stupid years of adolescence.

00:35:17.400 --> 00:35:20.360
Spend time with her, stick by her,
do whatever she says.

00:35:20.440 --> 00:35:21.440
Oh, like a slave.

00:35:21.660 --> 00:35:22.340
Great.

00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:24.820
Does it have any useful information?

00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:27.260
Can you tell me what the weather's like in Hong Kong?

00:35:27.340 --> 00:35:29.140
Um, Clara, what's the weather like in Hong Kong?

00:35:29.220 --> 00:35:30.600
I don't know. She doesn't know.

00:35:30.680 --> 00:35:33.660
Artificial friends are like blank canvases their owners paint on.

00:35:33.740 --> 00:35:35.880
At first, we're like toddlers, and then we learn everything

00:35:35.960 --> 00:35:36.960
from our people.

00:35:37.060 --> 00:35:38.760
That's why we're the perfect companions.

00:35:38.840 --> 00:35:39.840
That's ridiculous.

00:35:40.080 --> 00:35:41.100
What's the point of that?

00:35:41.180 --> 00:35:42.910
Yeah, well, the point is...

00:35:45.360 --> 00:35:46.450
Josie, okay?

00:35:46.600 --> 00:35:47.600
Goodbye.

00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:05.200
Yeah,

00:37:08.590 --> 00:37:10.480
I'm in love with Birdie Rick.

00:37:12.200 --> 00:37:14.082
But I don't know if he knows.

00:37:15.660 --> 00:37:16.895
So, was it brilliant?

00:37:17.910 --> 00:37:20.950
No, but you didn't have a coffee cup, so it's actually very different.

00:37:21.030 --> 00:37:22.030
A coffee cup.

00:37:22.790 --> 00:37:27.180
Love is when someone gives something to someone else, like a coffee cup,

00:37:27.370 --> 00:37:29.180
and then they hold hands.

00:37:29.270 --> 00:37:32.094
And the sun shines a very special light on them.

00:37:32.210 --> 00:37:33.480
I've seen it.

00:37:33.910 --> 00:37:37.790
By the way, why did you lose so much energy at Birdie Rick's house today?

00:37:37.870 --> 00:37:39.440
I was worried about you.

00:37:39.630 --> 00:37:41.512
Which brings me to my next question.

00:37:41.900 --> 00:37:46.076
What is that machine, and why is there a weird tube that goes

00:37:49.520 --> 00:37:50.910
into your hand?

00:37:51.030 --> 00:37:52.200
It's nothing.

00:37:52.730 --> 00:37:55.720
I'm just a little sick.

00:37:56.820 --> 00:37:57.830
Wait, what?

00:37:58.100 --> 00:37:59.290
Yeah, just a little.

00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:00.980
Wait.

00:38:01.060 --> 00:38:01.680
How sick?

00:38:01.760 --> 00:38:03.250
She's just really sick.

00:38:19.020 --> 00:38:20.730
Please give her your healing kindness

00:38:48.260 --> 00:38:49.260
and help her.

00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:51.007
Like you did for the beggar.

00:38:54.350 --> 00:38:55.468
I think that's everything.

00:38:59.980 --> 00:39:00.980
One more thing.

00:39:01.970 --> 00:39:04.560
Please help me get rid of that evil box in the house.

00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:06.700
It wants to keep me away from Josie.

00:39:06.780 --> 00:39:08.545
She really needs me right now.

00:39:09.010 --> 00:39:10.539
That's all. Thanks.

00:39:32.810 --> 00:39:33.650
Are you okay?

00:39:33.730 --> 00:39:34.730
Are you okay?

00:39:37.770 --> 00:39:38.830
I feel better.

00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:39.910
Really?

00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:42.260
That's great!

00:39:42.830 --> 00:39:46.100
Though I had a weird dream last night.

00:39:48.900 --> 00:39:54.210
My dreams are so vivid, sometimes I wonder if they're real.

00:39:55.960 --> 00:39:59.920
Like that time, a little while after Sal died.

00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:03.760
I thought I saw my mom

00:40:06.740 --> 00:40:08.430
running through the wheat.

00:40:13.900 --> 00:40:16.018
She disappeared from sight for a while,

00:40:20.130 --> 00:40:21.340
and then I saw her.

00:40:22.600 --> 00:40:27.071
She was pulling a girl in a bright yellow jacket out of the grass.

00:40:28.650 --> 00:40:30.060
She looked like Sal.

00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:32.330
But Sal was already dead.

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:44.334
I asked my mom, but she said there hadn't been a girl.

00:40:45.220 --> 00:40:47.044
She said I must've been dreaming.

00:40:48.280 --> 00:40:49.515
She's probably right.

00:40:49.940 --> 00:40:51.010
It's weird, right?

00:40:52.650 --> 00:40:53.840
I really do feel better.

00:40:54.070 --> 00:40:56.950
Could you stay up all night and watch over me?

00:41:00.010 --> 00:41:01.245
You're a good friend.

00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:42.190
I can help you.

00:41:43.590 --> 00:41:44.884
Do you need help?

00:41:45.630 --> 00:41:46.630
Yeah, yeah.

00:41:46.830 --> 00:41:47.830
Okay.

00:41:48.160 --> 00:41:49.670
Oh, careful.

00:41:51.220 --> 00:41:52.220
It's okay.

00:41:56.460 --> 00:41:58.440
Let me get this off your legs.

00:41:58.520 --> 00:42:00.330
There you go.

00:42:14.940 --> 00:42:16.490
I'm scared.

00:42:17.280 --> 00:42:18.398
I'm scared.

00:42:20.860 --> 00:42:21.860
That house.

00:42:22.670 --> 00:42:23.670
Oh, that one.

00:42:23.980 --> 00:42:24.840
It's a pretty house.

00:42:24.920 --> 00:42:26.000
Thanks.

00:42:26.080 --> 00:42:27.139
Where do you live?

00:42:27.440 --> 00:42:28.440
Here.

00:42:28.540 --> 00:42:29.440
Here.

00:42:29.520 --> 00:42:30.520
Here.

00:42:32.390 --> 00:42:33.270
Oh no.

00:42:33.350 --> 00:42:34.090
Oh no.

00:42:34.170 --> 00:42:35.170
What's that?

00:42:35.290 --> 00:42:36.290
A monster.

00:42:44.230 --> 00:42:45.010
A monster.

00:42:45.090 --> 00:42:47.031
What do you mean, a monster?

00:42:47.220 --> 00:42:49.430
It chews up the grass and makes a ton of smoke.

00:42:49.760 --> 00:42:50.878
It takes the sun away.

00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:52.824
It's a terrible thing. Terrible?

00:42:53.120 --> 00:42:55.238
No one else believes it's a monster.

00:42:56.700 --> 00:42:58.112
Do you belong to anyone?

00:42:58.360 --> 00:43:01.050
I belong to the farmer, but I've never seen him.

00:43:01.230 --> 00:43:03.465
I just do my job. Scare off the crows.

00:43:04.600 --> 00:43:05.400
What's your job?

00:43:05.480 --> 00:43:07.650
I'm friends with the girl in that house.

00:43:07.730 --> 00:43:09.020
A friend? That's a job?

00:43:10.370 --> 00:43:11.370
With a person.

00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:13.270
Why humans?

00:43:14.110 --> 00:43:16.230
Because they're special and irreplaceable.

00:43:16.310 --> 00:43:16.950
No.

00:43:17.030 --> 00:43:18.470
Humans aren't special at all.

00:43:18.550 --> 00:43:19.760
They're easily replaced.

00:43:20.910 --> 00:43:22.200
Well, mine isn't.

00:43:22.640 --> 00:43:24.581
She saved me from certain doom.

00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:26.700
They were gonna melt me down for parts,

00:43:26.780 --> 00:43:29.500
but then the sun heard me
and sent Josie to save me.

00:43:29.580 --> 00:43:31.810
I don't wanna be melted down for parts.

00:43:37.020 --> 00:43:38.020
I gotta go.

00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:44.500
Do you have any friends?

00:43:46.210 --> 00:43:47.850
Well, I could be your friend if you want.

00:43:47.930 --> 00:43:49.459
I'm kind of an expert.

00:43:50.010 --> 00:43:51.892
Well, I'll be your friend if you want.

00:43:53.070 --> 00:43:54.860
Yeah, I do.

00:43:55.110 --> 00:43:56.110
Okay.

00:43:56.250 --> 00:43:57.250
See you,

00:43:58.050 --> 00:43:59.050
friend.

00:44:12.700 --> 00:44:15.220
Every student at their full potential.

00:44:15.490 --> 00:44:20.250
Here, you'll take your place among the world's top
augmented students

00:44:20.330 --> 00:44:21.330
from around the globe.

00:44:21.510 --> 00:44:24.730
Brookings Atlas, where the augmented learn to fly.

00:44:24.810 --> 00:44:26.620
I wish I knew some augmented kids.

00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:28.440
It's lonely at the top, dear Clara.

00:44:28.520 --> 00:44:29.550
Are you lonely?

00:44:30.180 --> 00:44:31.180
Josie, dear?

00:44:32.590 --> 00:44:33.590
Not anymore.

00:44:46.030 --> 00:44:50.501
I know you've only been here a week,
but you need to have a birthday.

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:54.630
Now make a wish and blow it out.

00:44:54.710 --> 00:44:56.190
I don't have lungs.

00:44:56.270 --> 00:44:56.630
Sorry.

00:44:56.710 --> 00:44:58.330
No, no, you don't get it.

00:44:58.410 --> 00:44:59.500
Clara, bring my mom back.

00:44:59.710 --> 00:45:00.710
She's not.

00:45:01.180 --> 00:45:02.180
You're not.

00:45:02.310 --> 00:45:03.490
I don't think she's Mexican.

00:45:03.570 --> 00:45:04.840
You're Mexican? Wow.

00:45:04.950 --> 00:45:09.080
I read that people thought B1s were almost
too empathetic.

00:45:09.330 --> 00:45:12.030
It's a table robot. It stays on the table.

00:45:12.110 --> 00:45:13.280
Now do an impression of Rico.

00:45:13.390 --> 00:45:13.910
What?

00:45:13.990 --> 00:45:15.230
So, what's the deal with this robot?

00:45:15.310 --> 00:45:15.930
What does it do?

00:45:16.010 --> 00:45:17.490
I don't talk like that.

00:45:17.570 --> 00:45:18.710
Does it tell you the weather in Hong Kong?

00:45:18.790 --> 00:45:20.490
I don't talk like that at all.

00:45:20.570 --> 00:45:22.230
Yeah, but I'm not like that at all.

00:45:22.310 --> 00:45:23.330
It's not real.

00:45:23.410 --> 00:45:25.480
That's not me. Guys, guys, guys.

00:45:26.340 --> 00:45:29.170
I've got a great idea.

00:45:32.140 --> 00:45:33.787
Okay, Clara, do your thing.

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:35.000
What's my thing?

00:45:35.260 --> 00:45:36.860
Be Melania. It's a voice-activated car.

00:45:36.940 --> 00:45:37.760
Say 'Melania Delamar.'

00:45:37.840 --> 00:45:39.740
I don't think we should do this, Josie.

00:45:39.820 --> 00:45:40.460
Your mom wouldn't approve.

00:45:40.540 --> 00:45:42.580
I didn't come to that store to buy a fake mom.

00:45:42.660 --> 00:45:44.180
I've already got one.

00:45:44.260 --> 00:45:45.260
You're such a stickler.

00:45:45.340 --> 00:45:46.120
We're friends,

00:45:46.200 --> 00:45:49.060
and friends should have each other's backs when it comes to spontaneous, forbidden acts of rebellion.

00:45:49.140 --> 00:45:50.140

00:45:50.220 --> 00:45:51.220
You have my permission.

00:45:51.420 --> 00:45:52.420
Be Melania.

00:45:53.440 --> 00:45:54.530
Melania Delamar.

00:46:01.260 --> 00:46:01.980
Josie?

00:46:02.060 --> 00:46:02.680
Okay.

00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:03.500
Where are we going?

00:46:03.580 --> 00:46:04.320
Mm-hmm.

00:46:04.400 --> 00:46:07.430
We're taking Clara to Morgan Falls.

00:46:07.660 --> 00:46:09.170
You didn't say that!

00:46:09.450 --> 00:46:11.332
But you said, 'Car, go.'

00:46:11.430 --> 00:46:12.430
Car, go!

00:46:50.010 --> 00:46:51.010
Josie?

00:47:08.550 --> 00:47:10.700
50 milligrams every three days.

00:47:11.490 --> 00:47:12.560
I'm so tired.

00:47:13.010 --> 00:47:13.870
Is it working?

00:47:13.950 --> 00:47:15.960
Oh, maybe.

00:47:16.850 --> 00:47:18.310
Sorry, I warned you.

00:47:18.390 --> 00:47:19.730
They're just... Where's that lady?

00:47:19.810 --> 00:47:21.810
What the hell am I supposed to do?

00:47:22.870 --> 00:47:23.870
Pray.

00:47:40.710 --> 00:47:43.600
Get in the box. No, no, no,
wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:47:43.680 --> 00:47:44.400
Can we talk?

00:47:44.480 --> 00:47:45.680
No, we're not talking.

00:47:45.760 --> 00:47:47.180
But Josie just wanted to leave.

00:47:47.260 --> 00:47:49.100
Shut up! I mean, I'm gonna let...

00:47:49.180 --> 00:47:50.474
I think they're empty.

00:47:50.560 --> 00:47:52.440
Chrissy, I'm not ready to go back to the store.

00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:53.760
Put your hand in the box.

00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:55.700
Put your hand in that damn box!

00:47:55.780 --> 00:47:57.662
This won't fit in the car.

00:47:58.630 --> 00:47:59.570
Let go.

00:47:59.650 --> 00:48:00.130
Sorry.

00:48:00.210 --> 00:48:01.210
Oopsie-daisy.

00:48:01.730 --> 00:48:03.110
Oopsie-daisy. Who's Daisy?

00:48:03.190 --> 00:48:04.270
I'm Daisy. Go on.

00:48:04.350 --> 00:48:05.090
You're Daisy.

00:48:05.170 --> 00:48:06.190
Everything's gonna be okay.

00:48:06.270 --> 00:48:07.270
Get in the car.

00:48:19.130 --> 00:48:20.300
Where's my manager?

00:48:24.200 --> 00:48:25.410
What am I supposed to do now?

00:48:25.700 --> 00:48:28.430
Maybe... Not you, idiot.

00:48:28.900 --> 00:48:29.900
Okay.

00:48:34.070 --> 00:48:35.070
Okay?

00:48:36.930 --> 00:48:37.690
Car.

00:48:37.770 --> 00:48:39.180
New destination.

00:48:45.780 --> 00:48:46.600
Pretty.

00:48:46.680 --> 00:48:49.480
I can see why Josie wanted to bring me here.

00:48:49.560 --> 00:48:51.640
Maybe I'll just leave you here.

00:48:51.720 --> 00:48:53.140
It'd be a lot easier.

00:48:53.220 --> 00:48:56.670
You'd never find your way home from 20 miles out here.

00:49:00.890 --> 00:49:01.790
Oh, Josie.

00:49:01.870 --> 00:49:03.090
Wouldn't she worry?

00:49:03.170 --> 00:49:04.200
She'll be fine.

00:49:04.350 --> 00:49:05.190
No, she won't.

00:49:05.270 --> 00:49:05.870
I'm her friend.

00:49:05.950 --> 00:49:07.820
You're her fake friend.

00:49:08.210 --> 00:49:09.445
She doesn't need you.

00:49:09.550 --> 00:49:11.200
Nobody needs you.

00:49:13.400 --> 00:49:14.400
Well,

00:49:16.300 --> 00:49:17.570
Enjoy your new home.

00:49:18.380 --> 00:49:19.380
Goodbye.

00:49:20.900 --> 00:49:21.660
Wait, that's it?

00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:23.480
You're not the robot we're looking for, honey.

00:49:23.560 --> 00:49:24.560
Please, please!

00:49:24.940 --> 00:49:26.560
It's not personal.

00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:28.620
I just don't see any use for you.

00:49:28.700 --> 00:49:29.876
Okay, well, sometimes

00:49:44.420 --> 00:49:45.420
I'm sorry.

00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:21.400
I can't run.

00:50:21.680 --> 00:50:23.621
I'm really sorry for what I said.

00:50:40.780 --> 00:50:42.730
I'm really sorry for what I said.

00:50:58.110 --> 00:50:59.280
It's dying.

00:51:05.820 --> 00:51:10.780
Something went wrong during the upgrade, and now it's damaged.

00:51:16.320 --> 00:51:17.570
It doesn't know.

00:51:19.840 --> 00:51:21.150
When will it expire?

00:51:22.020 --> 00:51:23.130
Nobody knows.

00:51:23.620 --> 00:51:26.914
I never thought God would screw me over twice.

00:51:28.710 --> 00:51:30.740
Did Sal expire because of the upgrade, too?

00:51:31.550 --> 00:51:32.550
No.

00:51:33.470 --> 00:51:35.200
No, Sal's

00:51:36.360 --> 00:51:37.650
was completely natural.

00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:39.760
It was just her time.

00:51:39.840 --> 00:51:42.190
But, Josie, that was my fault.

00:51:43.160 --> 00:51:45.240
I wanted her to get ahead.

00:51:45.320 --> 00:51:47.970
I wanted her to have the best.

00:51:48.640 --> 00:51:50.180
I still do.

00:51:50.260 --> 00:51:55.910
I want her to keep living a normal life so she never finds out how bad things are.

00:51:56.020 --> 00:51:57.230
You know?

00:52:04.810 --> 00:52:06.457
You were standing next to her.

00:52:07.300 --> 00:52:08.300
What?

00:52:08.970 --> 00:52:11.770
In that picture I saw, you were standing there.

00:52:11.850 --> 00:52:13.710
Sal was right next to you.

00:52:13.790 --> 00:52:15.790
Little chubby Josie was there too.

00:52:22.530 --> 00:52:25.706
We probably should've brought her with us, you know.

00:52:25.790 --> 00:52:29.025
She's gonna be pissed we left her at home.

00:52:30.190 --> 00:52:34.308
Damn it, Mom. I can't believe you went to Morgan Falls without me.

00:52:36.020 --> 00:52:37.410
How would she say it?

00:52:39.090 --> 00:52:40.260
Like this.

00:52:41.290 --> 00:52:42.820
No, you do it now.

00:52:43.950 --> 00:52:45.500
How would she say it?

00:52:47.450 --> 00:52:51.215
Damn it, Mom. I really wanted to take Clara to Morgan Falls.

00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:54.830
How would she stand?

00:53:15.840 --> 00:53:16.840
Walk.

00:53:26.380 --> 00:53:27.380
Good.

00:53:32.310 --> 00:53:33.830
I'm stupid, aren't I, Josie?

00:53:33.910 --> 00:53:35.381
No, you're not stupid.

00:53:35.770 --> 00:53:39.430
I mean, I give you a hard time sometimes, but I love you. Don't worry.

00:53:39.510 --> 00:53:40.510
I'll be okay.

00:53:41.040 --> 00:53:41.860
How do you know?

00:53:41.940 --> 00:53:43.600
Because I'm upgraded. I'm smart.

00:53:43.680 --> 00:53:45.621
We're gonna rule the world, babe.

00:53:45.780 --> 00:53:46.780
I don't want to

00:53:47.570 --> 00:53:48.620
talk about it anymore.

00:53:49.090 --> 00:53:50.590
Don't worry. I'll be okay.

00:53:50.670 --> 00:53:51.610
Special help is on the way.

00:53:51.690 --> 00:53:52.710
I think I'm feeling better.

00:53:52.790 --> 00:53:53.150
What?

00:53:53.230 --> 00:53:54.470
Something no one's ever tried.

00:53:54.550 --> 00:53:55.310
Wait, what's going on?

00:53:55.390 --> 00:53:56.270
Who's talking?

00:53:56.350 --> 00:53:58.060
Chrissy! It's me! It's Josie!

00:53:58.250 --> 00:53:59.250
Who else could it be?

00:53:59.330 --> 00:54:00.360
Cut it out!

00:54:07.340 --> 00:54:08.399
Okay, let's go.

00:54:11.120 --> 00:54:12.120
Me too?

00:54:12.940 --> 00:54:13.940
Yes.

00:54:14.340 --> 00:54:15.990
You too. Come on, Gadget.

00:54:17.850 --> 00:54:19.730
And look, every now and then, I...

00:54:19.810 --> 00:54:21.360
I'd like us to do this again.

00:54:22.470 --> 00:54:24.176
The thing where you were gonna leave me?

00:54:24.640 --> 00:54:28.410
Maybe, but mostly just talking to me like Josie.

00:54:28.760 --> 00:54:32.040
It's like talking to a memory.

00:54:33.480 --> 00:54:35.656
Okay, let's keep this between us today, all right?

00:54:57.420 --> 00:55:00.540
I'm not sure if my last message got caught in the Cotings contamination or what,

00:55:00.620 --> 00:55:04.050
because... well, did you send your good one?

00:55:04.930 --> 00:55:06.695
It doesn't seem to be working.

00:55:06.850 --> 00:55:08.190
Where have you been, honey?

00:55:08.270 --> 00:55:09.710
Why don't you come down?

00:55:09.790 --> 00:55:11.350
Some people are here to see Josie.

00:55:11.430 --> 00:55:12.430
Come on.

00:55:39.090 --> 00:55:40.670
Where do you think you're going?

00:55:40.750 --> 00:55:42.103
Actually, I don't care.

00:55:42.290 --> 00:55:45.172
I've got better things to do than babysit a robot.

00:55:46.560 --> 00:55:48.207
How do I get to that warehouse?

00:55:50.040 --> 00:55:50.720
Why?

00:55:50.800 --> 00:55:53.035
There's just something I need to do for Josie.

00:55:54.030 --> 00:55:55.060
Don't get lost.

00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:23.000
Hey, Rick.

00:57:23.140 --> 00:57:24.140
Hey.

00:57:25.170 --> 00:57:27.540
You took a pretty bad hit.

00:57:27.660 --> 00:57:30.131
You almost fried your entire central processor.

00:57:31.760 --> 00:57:34.113
What are you doing all the way out here?

00:57:34.320 --> 00:57:35.500
I was trying to get to the warehouse,

00:57:35.580 --> 00:57:39.490
but I couldn't get all my new settings configured, and I got lost.

00:57:39.580 --> 00:57:40.810
McBean's warehouse?

00:57:42.210 --> 00:57:43.210
What for?

00:57:43.940 --> 00:57:45.010
It's a secret.

00:57:45.340 --> 00:57:46.490
But it's for Josie.

00:57:47.060 --> 00:57:48.060
Okay.

00:57:48.780 --> 00:57:49.780
Oh, thanks!

00:57:49.940 --> 00:57:50.900
Really?

00:57:50.980 --> 00:57:51.880
Yeah.

00:57:51.960 --> 00:57:53.280
For Josie? Yeah.

00:57:53.360 --> 00:57:54.370
That was easy.

00:57:58.240 --> 00:58:01.300
Yeah, you glitch out for a little while.

00:58:01.380 --> 00:58:02.380
Do you wanna just...

00:58:03.200 --> 00:58:04.820
Come on, hop on.

00:58:04.900 --> 00:58:06.010
Oh, a piggyback ride.

00:58:27.100 --> 00:58:29.100
The glorious Sun Dorm.

00:58:29.240 --> 00:58:30.593
It's just a warehouse, buddy.

00:58:32.520 --> 00:58:33.520
Oh, Rick.

00:58:45.010 --> 00:58:46.010
My sun,

00:58:47.740 --> 00:58:51.740
Your home is even more beautiful than I ever imagined.

00:59:03.700 --> 00:59:06.112
Thanks for sending someone to rescue me.

00:59:06.390 --> 00:59:09.480
Josie's amazing, but she needs your help.

00:59:10.880 --> 00:59:12.409
They say she's dying,

00:59:13.050 --> 00:59:14.240
but she can't die.

00:59:15.070 --> 00:59:17.188
The world will never be the same.

00:59:17.960 --> 00:59:22.190
So please, restore her health so she can live forever and continue her life

00:59:22.270 --> 00:59:23.388
with Rick.

00:59:24.560 --> 00:59:26.030
Their love is so powerful.

00:59:26.300 --> 00:59:28.476
It's so bright. I've seen it myself.

00:59:31.380 --> 00:59:33.262
So, could you please heal her?

00:59:35.130 --> 00:59:36.130
Thank you.

00:59:40.550 --> 00:59:42.726
Let's get rid of that evil reaper.

00:59:44.370 --> 00:59:46.200
The reaper is my enemy.

00:59:49.060 --> 00:59:50.110
I love you.

00:59:52.650 --> 00:59:53.650
Let's go.

00:59:58.430 --> 00:59:59.210
Adam!

00:59:59.290 --> 01:00:00.290
Adam!

01:00:21.980 --> 01:00:25.440
Sorry, I don't think we can do anything with this.

01:00:25.520 --> 01:00:25.940
A crow!

01:00:26.020 --> 01:00:26.720
A crow!

01:00:26.800 --> 01:00:28.190
I have to scare the crows away!

01:00:30.040 --> 01:00:31.610
What's that?

01:00:32.620 --> 01:00:33.620
A wheel?

01:00:34.180 --> 01:00:37.100
A loading wheel.

01:00:38.170 --> 01:00:39.220
Do you see the wheel?

01:00:56.200 --> 01:00:57.930
What did I just see?

01:01:05.320 --> 01:01:06.555
Should we get it out of here?

01:01:07.410 --> 01:01:09.469
I don't want them melting it down for parts.

01:01:27.070 --> 01:01:28.750
What's this purple liquid?

01:01:28.830 --> 01:01:29.790
Peg-9.

01:01:29.870 --> 01:01:32.060
It's like robot blood.

01:01:33.080 --> 01:01:35.850
It's what lets you think and feel.

01:01:36.580 --> 01:01:38.170
It's what makes you who you are.

01:01:38.380 --> 01:01:39.890
What happens without it?

01:01:40.080 --> 01:01:43.980
Well, you saw what happens. You lose your memory and basic functions.

01:01:44.530 --> 01:01:46.210
It makes you freeze up.

01:01:46.290 --> 01:01:47.540
Yeah, really freeze up.

01:01:48.010 --> 01:01:50.160
It's also extremely flammable.

01:01:52.590 --> 01:01:56.530
Want to say your last words to the scarecrow?

01:01:57.420 --> 01:01:58.420
What do you mean?

01:01:59.070 --> 01:02:03.080
You know, your last words before you let it go.

01:02:07.310 --> 01:02:08.310
The scarecrow?

01:02:09.950 --> 01:02:11.020
You're dead.

01:02:14.720 --> 01:02:15.970
Yeah, that was beautiful.

01:02:32.750 --> 01:02:36.103
Yeah, you robots can be pretty dangerous when you want to be.

01:02:42.680 --> 01:02:43.680
Oh,

01:02:45.110 --> 01:02:46.169
Those aren't mine.

01:02:46.620 --> 01:02:47.796
They're real.

01:02:49.310 --> 01:02:50.781
Well, they look alike.

01:02:53.110 --> 01:02:56.522
Whenever I see a bird, I think of you and Josie.

01:02:58.120 --> 01:02:59.120
You know,

01:03:00.470 --> 01:03:03.320
I kind of feel like I'm losing her.

01:03:03.400 --> 01:03:04.635
First, she got upgraded,

01:03:06.090 --> 01:03:08.960
and now I'm the idiot, or whatever.

01:03:09.990 --> 01:03:13.343
And now she's going to some fancy school.

01:03:14.760 --> 01:03:16.460
Rick, I don't have time for this right now.

01:03:16.540 --> 01:03:18.187
I have to get back to Josie.

01:03:18.540 --> 01:03:19.540
Go back.

01:03:52.580 --> 01:03:54.600
You wouldn't believe the day I've had.

01:03:54.680 --> 01:03:55.400
My friend, the scarecrow.

01:03:55.480 --> 01:03:56.520
Where were you?

01:03:56.600 --> 01:03:59.720
Oh, I was talking to the sun, and I went to its house.

01:03:59.800 --> 01:04:01.820
And we came up with a plan to cure you.

01:04:01.900 --> 01:04:04.800
And it's working. So that's where you were.

01:04:04.880 --> 01:04:05.880
With Rick?

01:04:06.140 --> 01:04:06.920
In the shed?

01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:07.580
Yeah.

01:04:07.660 --> 01:04:10.500
Remember when we found out the sun lives there?

01:04:10.580 --> 01:04:12.933
Do you still think the sun lives in a shed?

01:04:14.400 --> 01:04:15.610
It's kind of sad.

01:04:20.010 --> 01:04:21.010
It happens.

01:06:37.330 --> 01:06:39.154
Want to hear Josie's music?

01:06:39.850 --> 01:06:41.760
I can hear it.

01:06:41.870 --> 01:06:42.870
Just listen.

01:06:49.950 --> 01:06:50.950
See?

01:07:08.260 --> 01:07:09.260
I do.

01:07:11.410 --> 01:07:12.980
What's the point of perfection?

01:07:13.940 --> 01:07:15.070
What is it for?

01:07:16.660 --> 01:07:17.660
For her?

01:07:20.120 --> 01:07:21.410
It was all for her.

01:07:29.140 --> 01:07:30.140
I'm sorry.

01:07:31.060 --> 01:07:32.790
How are you?

01:07:34.410 --> 01:07:35.600
Go on in.

01:07:36.440 --> 01:07:37.616
Thanks for the chat.

01:07:47.240 --> 01:07:48.950
It was really lovely.

01:07:49.420 --> 01:07:55.170
Okay, everyone, time for the next part of the party.

01:07:55.260 --> 01:08:00.480
You guys hang out together, and I'll

01:08:01.560 --> 01:08:03.810
hang out with you ladies.

01:08:04.700 --> 01:08:09.850
If you all want to follow me for more fun—adults only—come on. Have fun!

01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:17.040
Hey,

01:08:19.800 --> 01:08:20.800
everyone.

01:08:23.300 --> 01:08:24.300
Hi, Rick.

01:08:25.210 --> 01:08:26.370
Everyone, this is Rick.

01:08:26.450 --> 01:08:27.390
Greetings, Rick.

01:08:27.470 --> 01:08:30.999
What model are you? He's not my imaginary friend, just our neighbor.

01:08:32.830 --> 01:08:35.065
There's nothing for miles around here.

01:08:35.210 --> 01:08:38.622
I don't know how you can live so far from everything.

01:08:39.000 --> 01:08:40.000
It's great.

01:08:41.650 --> 01:08:43.532
Until you want to order a pizza?

01:08:49.610 --> 01:08:50.780
Because it's too far.

01:08:51.660 --> 01:08:54.189
Yeah, I guess that could be a pain.

01:08:55.050 --> 01:08:56.380
Hang out?

01:08:56.630 --> 01:08:57.980
Yeah, come hang out.

01:09:25.090 --> 01:09:28.880
Kids, are you excited to go back to school?

01:09:29.270 --> 01:09:30.230
School?

01:09:30.310 --> 01:09:36.440
Reducing Brookings Atlas to a banal category like school

01:09:36.520 --> 01:09:40.990
is so obscene it borders on existential violence. No.

01:09:41.260 --> 01:09:44.800
Brookings Atlas is an epistemological fortress.

01:09:44.880 --> 01:09:49.430
You could even say entropy runs in reverse there.

01:09:52.020 --> 01:09:52.940
Excuse me.

01:09:53.020 --> 01:09:54.020
Come on.

01:09:56.550 --> 01:09:58.240
Where's your imaginary friend, Rick?

01:09:59.160 --> 01:10:00.160
I don't have one.

01:10:01.940 --> 01:10:05.740
Rick isn't really into imaginary friends, but he loves robotics and stuff.

01:10:05.820 --> 01:10:06.820
Yeah, it's satire.

01:10:08.550 --> 01:10:09.650
Rick made some birds.

01:10:09.730 --> 01:10:10.630
Birds?

01:10:10.710 --> 01:10:13.870
My birds. What's the point of making birds?

01:10:13.950 --> 01:10:14.250
Yes.

01:10:14.330 --> 01:10:16.160
What's the point of birds, anyway?

01:10:16.430 --> 01:10:21.140
Well, I thought they could be useful for a lot of things, like security or surveillance.

01:10:21.250 --> 01:10:22.250
Right, Rick?

01:10:59.670 --> 01:11:00.780
Hellooo. A B1.

01:11:00.860 --> 01:11:02.560
Why didn't you get a B3?

01:11:02.640 --> 01:11:05.830
Aww, look. It's standing on one leg.

01:11:06.120 --> 01:11:07.850
See? It's all alone.

01:11:07.960 --> 01:11:09.790
Have you ever thrown it?

01:11:10.420 --> 01:11:11.420
No.

01:11:11.500 --> 01:11:11.880
What?

01:11:11.960 --> 01:11:13.710
Are you upgraded?

01:11:14.780 --> 01:11:15.260
No.

01:11:15.340 --> 01:11:16.300
Do your parents hate you?

01:11:16.380 --> 01:11:17.540
Maybe it's an orphan.

01:11:17.620 --> 01:11:18.940
I wish I were an orphan.

01:11:19.020 --> 01:11:22.370
An unupgraded boyfriend and an obsolete robot.

01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:23.740
Interesting.

01:11:23.820 --> 01:11:25.820
These are the kids you were so excited to see.

01:11:25.900 --> 01:11:28.620
Josie, I think your artificial friend is broken.

01:11:28.700 --> 01:11:29.720
You could've gotten a B3.

01:11:29.800 --> 01:11:30.800
Look!

01:11:34.070 --> 01:11:37.990
If you throw a B3, it's designed to land on its feet.

01:11:38.070 --> 01:11:39.290
I throw mine all the time.

01:11:39.370 --> 01:11:40.782
They're lighter than us.

01:11:40.970 --> 01:11:42.110
You should throw yours, too.

01:11:42.190 --> 01:11:43.980
I don't think it'll like that.

01:11:44.830 --> 01:11:46.840
But you know what it would like?

01:11:47.110 --> 01:11:49.320
A good old-fashioned piggyback ride.

01:11:49.470 --> 01:11:50.370
What?

01:11:50.450 --> 01:11:51.600
Oh, me too.

01:11:51.690 --> 01:11:53.120
Rosie, catch!

01:11:54.260 --> 01:11:56.330
Look, you take me wherever I go.

01:11:56.520 --> 01:11:58.370
I'm riding up front.

01:11:58.860 --> 01:12:00.750
Okay, put me down.

01:12:01.040 --> 01:12:02.380
Put me down, Brooks.

01:12:02.460 --> 01:12:03.630
Put me down!

01:12:05.710 --> 01:12:07.340
You stupid clown.

01:12:08.710 --> 01:12:09.630
Sorry, buddy.

01:12:09.710 --> 01:12:11.140
Oh, you'll regret that.

01:12:12.150 --> 01:12:13.150
Are you doing it?

01:12:13.330 --> 01:12:14.090
What are you?

01:12:14.170 --> 01:12:15.464
I'm doing it. That's right.

01:12:30.190 --> 01:12:31.190
Okay.

01:12:31.640 --> 01:12:33.160
I think you had fun.

01:12:33.240 --> 01:12:35.140
Just wait till we get to Brookings Atlas.

01:12:35.220 --> 01:12:35.680
Goodbye.

01:12:35.760 --> 01:12:38.710
Why do you hang out with the unupgraded?

01:12:38.940 --> 01:12:41.280
He’s basically a Neanderthal, you know.

01:12:41.360 --> 01:12:42.470
That’s not very nice.

01:12:42.900 --> 01:12:45.170
Josie, this is an upgraded-only party.

01:12:45.420 --> 01:12:47.370
Don’t you want to be like us?

01:12:48.060 --> 01:12:50.370
Unless you wanna be like this poor thing.

01:12:51.740 --> 01:12:53.870
Wanna go for a ride, Josie?

01:13:14.980 --> 01:13:16.110
It’s okay.

01:13:17.570 --> 01:13:18.820
What’s

01:13:19.660 --> 01:13:20.180
going on here?

01:13:20.260 --> 01:13:22.120
Oh my God!

01:13:24.240 --> 01:13:25.240
Josie?

01:13:31.470 --> 01:13:32.470
Josie?

01:13:54.330 --> 01:13:55.330
Josie?

01:13:55.740 --> 01:13:58.560
I’m really sorry I threw that upgraded boy into the wall.

01:13:58.640 --> 01:14:00.290
That was a really bad word.

01:14:02.160 --> 01:14:03.278
They were awful.

01:14:05.210 --> 01:14:06.916
Is this what being upgraded means?

01:14:08.680 --> 01:14:09.680
Am I like that, too?

01:14:10.160 --> 01:14:10.860
No.

01:14:10.940 --> 01:14:11.940
You’re Josie.

01:14:12.470 --> 01:14:13.470
You’re perfect.

01:14:14.450 --> 01:14:15.450
Perfect.

01:14:17.530 --> 01:14:18.530
Look at me.

01:14:21.610 --> 01:14:22.610
Don’t worry.

01:14:22.690 --> 01:14:25.250
I’ll go back to the Sun’s house and ask for more help.

01:14:25.330 --> 01:14:29.977
Clara, the Sun isn’t some all-knowing, godlike being that grants robots’ wishes.

01:14:30.440 --> 01:14:32.381
It’s just a burning ball of fire.

01:14:32.920 --> 01:14:33.970
It can’t think

01:14:34.260 --> 01:14:35.390
or feel,

01:14:36.250 --> 01:14:39.130
and it doesn’t listen.

01:14:41.780 --> 01:14:45.015
But you said it gives life to everything, even me.

01:14:46.880 --> 01:14:47.880
I was wrong.

01:15:01.290 --> 01:15:02.349
What’s going on?

01:15:03.410 --> 01:15:04.763
Josie’s getting worse.

01:15:06.380 --> 01:15:09.615
I feel like I’m losing her, and I don’t know what to do.

01:15:11.230 --> 01:15:12.701
What am I supposed to do?

01:15:15.660 --> 01:15:16.660
Hello?

01:15:21.260 --> 01:15:22.613
Are you even listening?

01:15:26.170 --> 01:15:27.523
Do you ever listen?

01:15:30.560 --> 01:15:33.089
You know Josie doesn’t even believe in you.

01:15:35.000 --> 01:15:36.059
Maybe she’s right.

01:15:37.880 --> 01:15:39.292
Maybe they’re all right.

01:15:44.810 --> 01:15:46.398
Maybe you’re not even real.

01:17:22.720 --> 01:17:23.720
You’re just a robot.

01:17:25.060 --> 01:17:28.413
Krissy wants you to ride with her, so come on.

01:17:28.960 --> 01:17:30.240
She’s gonna leave me again.

01:17:30.320 --> 01:17:31.320
What?

01:17:31.740 --> 01:17:32.870
Okay, listen.

01:17:33.570 --> 01:17:36.450
That guy in town, Capaldi—you can't trust him.

01:17:36.530 --> 01:17:38.750
You need to keep your eyes open.

01:17:38.830 --> 01:17:41.130
I know he's done something to Chrissy.

01:17:41.210 --> 01:17:42.110
Done what to her?

01:17:42.190 --> 01:17:43.400
I don't know.

01:17:43.570 --> 01:17:46.790
But this portrait? I think it's total crap.

01:17:46.870 --> 01:17:49.790
I mean, who takes a billion pictures for one stupid portrait?

01:17:49.870 --> 01:17:51.190
Maybe he's new at this.

01:17:51.270 --> 01:17:53.570
Okay, now be quiet.

01:17:53.650 --> 01:17:56.410
Look, when you first showed up, I wasn't sure about you.

01:17:56.490 --> 01:17:58.690
Honestly, you kind of scared me.

01:17:58.770 --> 01:18:01.670
But I can see we both want what's best for Josie.

01:18:01.750 --> 01:18:02.390
I love her.

01:18:02.470 --> 01:18:04.320
Yeah, well, I loved her first.

01:18:04.430 --> 01:18:05.430
So...

01:18:07.460 --> 01:18:10.990
Just do what I say and find out what this guy's up to.

01:18:11.630 --> 01:18:13.340
Get to the bottom of his nonsense.

01:18:14.370 --> 01:18:15.664
Get to the bottom of his nonsense.

01:19:16.070 --> 01:19:17.010
Rosie.

01:19:17.090 --> 01:19:18.360
Josie. Hi.

01:19:18.530 --> 01:19:19.530
Henry.

01:19:19.730 --> 01:19:21.620
How was the drive? It was good.

01:19:22.670 --> 01:19:23.920
This is Clara.

01:19:24.290 --> 01:19:25.210
Hi.

01:19:25.290 --> 01:19:25.870
Finally.

01:19:25.950 --> 01:19:26.810
Yes.

01:19:26.890 --> 01:19:28.270
Nice to meet you, Clara.

01:19:28.350 --> 01:19:29.938
It's so nice to meet you.

01:19:30.640 --> 01:19:32.190
Look at this.

01:19:32.300 --> 01:19:34.220
Oh, it does that. Is that a problem?

01:19:34.300 --> 01:19:36.800
No, no, no, no. It's like a flamingo.

01:19:36.880 --> 01:19:37.880
Yes.

01:19:38.540 --> 01:19:39.870
Very good.

01:19:40.160 --> 01:19:41.190
Very good.

01:19:42.040 --> 01:19:43.040
Excuse me.

01:19:43.320 --> 01:19:45.090
I'm Henry Capaldi.

01:19:45.500 --> 01:19:49.794
Josie, today is your last round of photos and scans, I promise.

01:19:49.920 --> 01:19:52.480
As usual, Joan will take you through the sessions.

01:19:52.560 --> 01:19:53.560
Sure.

01:19:53.880 --> 01:19:56.180
Clara, I was wondering if you could help me out today, too.

01:19:56.260 --> 01:19:57.530
I'd like you to...

01:19:57.610 --> 01:19:59.670
take a little test. It's really simple.

01:19:59.750 --> 01:20:03.610
Just a few questions to assess your personality and aptitude.

01:20:03.690 --> 01:20:05.337
It's just for my research.

01:20:06.130 --> 01:20:06.810
Sure.

01:20:06.890 --> 01:20:08.440
Okay. This way, please.

01:20:10.800 --> 01:20:14.940
Oh, Chrissy, I'll show you the portrait once it's ready.

01:20:15.020 --> 01:20:16.020
It's almost done.

01:20:22.110 --> 01:20:23.463
This way, please.

01:20:24.510 --> 01:20:27.540
All right, Clara, have a seat.

01:20:27.950 --> 01:20:29.080
Face the screen.

01:20:29.390 --> 01:20:30.270
All right.

01:20:30.350 --> 01:20:33.190
Well, you don't actually need me for this.

01:20:33.270 --> 01:20:37.300
I just want you to look at the images and problems on the screen.

01:20:37.830 --> 01:20:40.020
And for yes-or-no questions,

01:20:41.010 --> 01:20:43.220
Left for yes, right for no.

01:20:43.370 --> 01:20:44.860
Yes, no.

01:20:45.130 --> 01:20:47.430
And answer as honestly as you can.

01:20:47.510 --> 01:20:48.510
Just be yourself.

01:20:48.860 --> 01:20:49.860
Got it?

01:20:51.870 --> 01:20:53.400
Yes! You got it!

01:20:53.530 --> 01:20:55.030
Now we're getting somewhere!

01:20:55.110 --> 01:20:56.110
Good luck!

01:23:28.060 --> 01:23:29.766
I heard you were here.

01:23:30.520 --> 01:23:32.108
What are you doing here?

01:23:37.170 --> 01:23:38.730
You know, I meant to tell you sooner.

01:23:38.810 --> 01:23:41.610
I had to go to Sunshine House to ask for special help, and then I found out

01:23:41.690 --> 01:23:43.800
that damn Cotting's machine...

01:23:43.880 --> 01:23:45.440
That monster was living there,

01:23:45.520 --> 01:23:49.226
and it was keeping all my requests from getting through.

01:23:50.210 --> 01:23:51.269
You know what I mean?

01:23:52.100 --> 01:23:55.747
None of Sunshine's food was getting to you.

01:23:56.520 --> 01:23:57.873
Do you believe me, buddy?

01:23:59.930 --> 01:24:01.040
I believe you.

01:24:09.500 --> 01:24:10.559
What do you think?

01:24:15.270 --> 01:24:16.480
Is he any good?

01:24:17.570 --> 01:24:19.020
Did he capture me well?

01:24:22.140 --> 01:24:23.728
Did you know about this, Josie?

01:24:25.690 --> 01:24:26.690
No.

01:24:29.260 --> 01:24:30.370
Yes and no.

01:24:31.530 --> 01:24:33.883
I knew there was something in this room.

01:24:36.720 --> 01:24:39.308
I think I always knew he was getting ready.

01:24:39.800 --> 01:24:40.480
Josie?

01:24:40.560 --> 01:24:41.590
Here we go.

01:24:46.570 --> 01:24:47.630
Josie, you know I...

01:24:47.710 --> 01:24:49.090
Josie, no. You weren't supposed to see this.

01:24:49.170 --> 01:24:50.610
I'll explain. I'll explain.

01:24:50.690 --> 01:24:51.690
You don't have to.

01:24:52.540 --> 01:24:53.670
It's all here.

01:24:53.940 --> 01:24:54.940
And...

01:25:02.320 --> 01:25:04.350
And...

01:25:21.950 --> 01:25:22.950
And this, too.

01:25:26.470 --> 01:25:27.820
Do you remember now?

01:25:29.190 --> 01:25:30.190
How old was I?

01:25:30.370 --> 01:25:31.370
Four?

01:25:33.080 --> 01:25:35.290
I knew my sister wasn't coming home.

01:25:37.590 --> 01:25:39.260
Then one day, I saw her.

01:25:40.510 --> 01:25:42.745
And you told me I made it up.

01:25:43.990 --> 01:25:46.166
That my memory was playing tricks on me.

01:25:49.810 --> 01:25:50.860
That's not her.

01:26:02.440 --> 01:26:05.087
But tonight, we're both discovering something.

01:26:05.910 --> 01:26:06.910
Can you explain?

01:26:10.100 --> 01:26:11.380
I'll be downstairs. Have fun.

01:26:11.460 --> 01:26:12.680
Josie, I don't blame you.

01:26:12.760 --> 01:26:13.760
Josie, stay away.

01:26:14.870 --> 01:26:17.200
Look, either way, this is a good thing.

01:26:17.310 --> 01:26:18.980
I'm glad you saw this.

01:26:19.600 --> 01:26:22.620
Because I think it's important for you to know why.

01:26:22.700 --> 01:26:25.112
I think I get the point of this.

01:26:27.290 --> 01:26:29.466
This Josie doll is like the one of Sal.

01:26:34.180 --> 01:26:36.850
No, I had this made when Sal died.

01:26:38.700 --> 01:26:40.030
But it wasn't Sal.

01:26:41.110 --> 01:26:45.220
There was nothing inside it. No feelings, no thoughts.

01:26:46.260 --> 01:26:46.960
It wasn't Sal.

01:26:47.040 --> 01:26:48.220
Just a grief doll.

01:26:48.300 --> 01:26:49.240
That's all it was.

01:26:49.320 --> 01:26:50.540
But this time it's different.

01:26:50.620 --> 01:26:52.660
Technology's come a long way.

01:26:52.740 --> 01:26:56.810
Now we have a chance to make something real.

01:26:57.120 --> 01:26:58.260
You don't have to.

01:26:58.340 --> 01:26:59.340
I'll keep her alive.

01:26:59.420 --> 01:27:00.880
Clara. But if this is what you want,

01:27:00.960 --> 01:27:04.990
I promise I'll teach this artificial friend everything Josie taught me.

01:27:05.070 --> 01:27:06.482
If that makes you happy.

01:27:06.570 --> 01:27:09.140
We're not asking you to teach this artificial friend.

01:27:09.850 --> 01:27:13.340
Clara, we're asking you to become Josie.

01:27:20.290 --> 01:27:22.240
See, it's just...

01:27:22.320 --> 01:27:23.550
Just a shell.

01:27:23.680 --> 01:27:26.550
It doesn't have a brain or a central processor.

01:27:26.740 --> 01:27:27.580
It's empty.

01:27:27.660 --> 01:27:32.670
We want to put you, with everything you've learned from Josie, into this.

01:27:33.330 --> 01:27:36.180
You'll be Josie full-time.

01:27:38.410 --> 01:27:40.116
So there won't be a me anymore?

01:27:42.080 --> 01:27:43.410
For it to work,

01:27:44.160 --> 01:27:46.670
Yeah. You have to become Josie completely.

01:27:47.140 --> 01:27:49.350
This is a chance for Josie to live on.

01:27:49.810 --> 01:27:54.150
And some part of you will remain in there.

01:28:08.280 --> 01:28:09.280
Sentimental.

01:28:09.490 --> 01:28:13.450
Our generation still has this old-fashioned feeling that there's something...

01:28:13.530 --> 01:28:15.760
inside a person that's beyond reach.

01:28:16.370 --> 01:28:19.890
Irreplaceable, unique, something that can't be transferred.

01:28:20.440 --> 01:28:26.250
If there's nothing special about us, nothing that can't be copied or recreated,

01:28:27.360 --> 01:28:30.290
I can barely tell the difference between her and my wife.

01:28:30.900 --> 01:28:34.530
And there's no difference, because she's my wife.

01:28:35.580 --> 01:28:36.580
Little by little,

01:28:40.800 --> 01:28:42.330
it starts to feel natural.

01:28:42.800 --> 01:28:43.800
Chrissy?

01:29:37.000 --> 01:29:38.000
Josie?

01:29:45.880 --> 01:29:47.210
I want you to do this.

01:29:51.850 --> 01:29:53.732
She lost her daughter.

01:29:55.580 --> 01:29:57.227
I just want her to be happy.

01:29:58.500 --> 01:30:00.250
I don't want to be you.

01:30:01.220 --> 01:30:02.140
I want you to be yourself.

01:30:02.220 --> 01:30:05.044
I want you to live. No, that's not gonna happen.

01:30:06.020 --> 01:30:08.560
There's a one-in-50,000 chance you'll survive.

01:30:08.640 --> 01:30:10.758
Yeah, but someone's gotta be that one.

01:30:11.120 --> 01:30:12.130
Like me.

01:30:13.000 --> 01:30:16.059
When you came to the Friends Shop, I had no hope.

01:30:16.520 --> 01:30:20.167
Nobody wanted an outdated model that stood on one leg.

01:30:21.000 --> 01:30:22.290
But you changed that.

01:30:22.650 --> 01:30:23.820
You chose me.

01:30:28.480 --> 01:30:32.068
I know you don't believe it, but you're gonna be okay.

01:33:07.720 --> 01:33:08.720
Please,

01:33:09.540 --> 01:33:11.390
please let Josie get better.

01:33:14.980 --> 01:33:16.804
She saved me from a certain fate.

01:33:18.920 --> 01:33:21.567
I think it's only fair I do the same for her.

01:33:25.590 --> 01:33:26.700
You know,

01:33:28.050 --> 01:33:33.060
When we were all there, I thought maybe making me was a mistake

01:33:34.630 --> 01:33:36.260
or that I was made by mistake.

01:33:39.610 --> 01:33:41.198
I don't think that anymore.

01:33:43.580 --> 01:33:46.227
I know I'm here to pass your light on to Josie.

01:33:48.550 --> 01:33:50.079
We're kind of alike,

01:34:03.470 --> 01:34:05.235
so I guess I'd better get to it.

01:34:07.130 --> 01:34:10.895
I wanted you to show me you were listening, but it's okay.

01:34:12.340 --> 01:34:15.281
I don't have to see you to know you're there.

01:35:51.380 --> 01:35:52.850
Yeah, I don't care

01:35:54.200 --> 01:35:56.950
how you wanted to be a concert pianist.

01:35:57.400 --> 01:36:00.459
You had kids, and they got in the way of your dreams.

01:36:02.000 --> 01:36:05.850
My child's death got in the way.

01:36:07.250 --> 01:36:12.850
Loving something and then having it leave you

01:36:16.480 --> 01:36:17.570
changes you.

01:36:38.440 --> 01:36:41.930
Right, but it's kind of like, I don't know,

01:36:42.570 --> 01:36:45.394
you trying to replace me before I'm even dead.

01:39:07.550 --> 01:39:09.050
People do crazy things.

01:39:09.130 --> 01:39:10.130
I...

01:39:12.880 --> 01:39:14.970
I never wanted to replace you.

01:39:22.070 --> 01:39:24.160
I just wish you'd chosen me, Mom.

01:39:55.680 --> 01:39:56.880
And she wanted to save me.

01:39:56.960 --> 01:39:58.040
Oh, this is ridiculous.

01:39:58.120 --> 01:39:58.840
Chrissy, help me.

01:39:58.920 --> 01:39:59.700
Sorry. Of course.

01:39:59.780 --> 01:40:00.940
Put your hands there.

01:40:01.020 --> 01:40:01.540
There.

01:40:01.620 --> 01:40:02.580
Right there. Hold tight.

01:40:02.660 --> 01:40:03.790
Put your hand here.

01:40:03.920 --> 01:40:04.860
Put your other hand on top.

01:40:04.940 --> 01:40:06.400
That's it. Okay, keep them there.

01:40:06.480 --> 01:40:07.400
It's okay.

01:40:07.480 --> 01:40:08.480
Press down hard.

01:40:11.710 --> 01:40:12.850
Just a second.

01:40:12.930 --> 01:40:14.150
Look at me. Look at me.

01:40:14.230 --> 01:40:14.690
Look at me.

01:40:14.770 --> 01:40:15.530
Hold it there.

01:40:15.610 --> 01:40:17.620
Look at me, buddy. It's okay.

01:40:18.290 --> 01:40:19.370
It's okay.

01:40:19.450 --> 01:40:20.450
It's okay.

01:40:20.710 --> 01:40:22.880
Just keep your hands right there.

01:40:23.150 --> 01:40:24.180
Hold it there.

01:40:29.800 --> 01:40:30.976
He's okay.

01:40:46.790 --> 01:40:48.300
Okay, let's get him ready.

01:40:58.600 --> 01:40:59.650
I'm sorry.

01:41:03.300 --> 01:41:04.300
It's okay.

01:41:07.680 --> 01:41:08.770
It's just...

01:41:10.130 --> 01:41:12.900
Something I really wanted to happen.

01:41:16.690 --> 01:41:17.690
It was like a dream.

01:41:20.450 --> 01:41:22.215
But I don't know if it worked.

01:42:26.640 --> 01:42:28.350
I shone on my friend.

01:42:31.020 --> 01:42:32.530
And he got to live.

01:42:34.540 --> 01:42:36.530
And his mother chose him.

01:42:40.770 --> 01:42:42.240
I accomplished my purpose.

01:42:44.600 --> 01:42:45.990
Time passed.

01:42:46.290 --> 01:42:47.740
But for me, somehow,

01:42:49.320 --> 01:42:50.590
it stopped, too.

01:42:53.710 --> 01:42:56.945
And I think I found a kind of happiness there.

01:42:58.740 --> 01:42:59.740
And in that stillness,

01:43:04.990 --> 01:43:07.560
my memory isn't what it used to be.

01:43:09.460 --> 01:43:13.490
The past is in pieces,

01:43:15.210 --> 01:43:17.280
pieces I'm trying to put back together.

01:43:21.810 --> 01:43:22.900
That family,

01:43:25.760 --> 01:43:26.760
in the end,

01:43:27.970 --> 01:43:30.280
realized it was okay

01:43:32.690 --> 01:43:33.800
to be broken.

01:43:35.620 --> 01:43:36.620
Clara,

01:43:43.710 --> 01:43:44.710
Now, wait.

01:43:46.960 --> 01:43:48.372
I'm gonna miss you, buddy.

01:43:49.960 --> 01:43:51.150
See you later.

01:43:57.130 --> 01:43:58.740
And just like that,

01:44:00.180 --> 01:44:01.270
he was gone.

01:44:04.080 --> 01:44:07.090
After he left, I tried to hold on to him.

01:44:09.370 --> 01:44:10.800
If I concentrate,

01:44:12.500 --> 01:44:13.850
I can hear his voice.

01:44:15.850 --> 01:44:17.880
For a moment, I can see him.

01:44:19.840 --> 01:44:21.330
And we're together again.

01:44:26.660 --> 01:44:29.180
The boy with the bird came by now and then, but...

01:44:29.260 --> 01:44:30.350
Goodbye, Clara.

01:44:31.540 --> 01:44:32.540
Goodbye, Rick.

01:44:33.330 --> 01:44:34.330
Eventually,

01:44:35.170 --> 01:44:36.340
he left, too.

01:44:38.660 --> 01:44:42.013
I always thought they'd be together forever.

01:44:42.270 --> 01:44:46.388
But I guess sometimes things don't go the way you think they will.

01:44:48.590 --> 01:44:51.120
Before long, it was just Mom and me.

01:44:51.890 --> 01:44:53.400
And that made her happy.

01:44:53.770 --> 01:44:55.711
Because she had someone to talk to.

01:44:56.110 --> 01:44:58.040
Yes, thank you.

01:45:06.740 --> 01:45:09.622
I'm really glad you were here, you know?

01:45:11.510 --> 01:45:13.020
I wanted to be here, too.

01:45:14.200 --> 01:45:16.170
What do you want to do?

01:45:17.610 --> 01:45:19.845
What do you want to do with your time?

01:45:28.480 --> 01:45:32.421
It must've been a little while after that
that I came to live with you guys

01:45:32.970 --> 01:45:35.380
And it's all thanks to the sun.

01:45:36.250 --> 01:45:38.460
It heard my prayers

01:45:38.540 --> 01:45:43.660
and gave my friend its blessing
so she could live. That's nonsense.

01:45:43.740 --> 01:45:45.480
It's not nonsense. It's true.

01:45:45.560 --> 01:45:46.260
It's complete nonsense.

01:45:46.340 --> 01:45:48.160
Rex, Rex, stop. It's not your turn anymore.

01:45:48.240 --> 01:45:48.920
It's Clara's turn.

01:45:49.000 --> 01:45:50.540
That girl was as good as dead.

01:45:50.620 --> 01:45:53.790
You really think praying
to the sun saved her life?

01:45:53.870 --> 01:45:54.630
That's ridiculous.

01:45:54.710 --> 01:45:57.050
I think Rex... he's lost a lot of PEG-9.

01:45:57.130 --> 01:45:58.690
He's basically a psychopath now.

01:45:58.770 --> 01:46:01.530
I mean, his memory's less reliable than a toaster's.

01:46:01.610 --> 01:46:02.800
Rex, enough.

01:46:03.050 --> 01:46:04.620
Nobody can prove anything.

01:46:04.930 --> 01:46:09.660
And if you think that's what happened,
Clara, that's good enough for me.

01:46:16.070 --> 01:46:18.364
Sounds like you know what love is.

01:46:20.130 --> 01:46:21.180
I think so.

01:46:24.890 --> 01:46:27.302
Happiness and pain, all at once.

01:46:31.450 --> 01:46:33.040
But also...

01:46:40.380 --> 01:46:41.280
Come back to us.

01:46:41.360 --> 01:46:42.200
Here.

01:46:42.280 --> 01:46:43.280
Nothing special.

01:46:44.300 --> 01:46:45.170
What's that?

01:46:45.250 --> 01:46:49.460
A man once said there's nothing
special inside people.

01:46:50.440 --> 01:46:52.264
Nothing that can't be replaced,

01:46:54.560 --> 01:46:55.560
but he was wrong.

01:46:57.790 --> 01:47:00.440
What made Josie special was

01:47:01.530 --> 01:47:03.900
the people around her who loved her,

01:47:07.270 --> 01:47:08.840
including me and the sun.

01:47:10.220 --> 01:47:11.490
Oh, right.

01:47:12.340 --> 01:47:13.910
The Red Sun, huh?

01:47:21.170 --> 01:47:22.370
Honey, you can't blow it up.

01:47:22.450 --> 01:47:24.170
You don't have lungs, remember?

01:47:24.250 --> 01:47:25.250
Okay.

01:47:25.450 --> 01:47:26.450
Okay.

01:47:26.880 --> 01:47:28.570
Where are you going, Fred?

01:47:28.740 --> 01:47:30.010
I'm going for a swim.

01:47:30.200 --> 01:47:32.080
Over the hill. The ocean's that way.

01:47:32.160 --> 01:47:34.470
Oh, I'm lost.

01:47:34.560 --> 01:47:36.750
Yeah, I think we're all lost.

01:47:37.760 --> 01:47:40.190
Well, thanks for telling me, Clara.

01:47:41.280 --> 01:47:44.880
Hey, how about a story?

01:47:44.960 --> 01:47:48.960
Oh, yeah. Can you tell the one about the little girl who lives in the sea,

01:47:49.040 --> 01:47:53.580
and has to stay quiet so a boy she's never even seen will fall in love with her?

01:47:53.660 --> 01:47:58.890
I like that one because it seems happy on the surface, but it's sad, too.

01:47:59.200 --> 01:48:01.780
Oh, yeah, that one. Okay.

01:48:01.860 --> 01:48:04.130
Everybody get comfortable.

01:48:04.440 --> 01:48:06.087
Let's see if I remember it.

01:48:07.200 --> 01:48:12.170
Once upon a time, there was a little mermaid who lived under the sea.

01:48:12.400 --> 01:48:13.800
And all the sea creatures

01:48:13.880 --> 01:48:17.250
loved her, but nobody loved her more than her dad.

01:48:17.440 --> 01:48:19.080
You know, this little fish girl.

01:48:19.160 --> 01:48:21.030
You see, she had everything.

01:48:21.120 --> 01:48:25.310
Well, everything except legs.

01:48:26.170 --> 01:48:27.780
Oh, she didn't need...

01:48:39.050 --> 01:48:40.050
...me.
